<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- App Store distribution, uploaded straight to App Store Connect. -->
    <key>method</key>
    <string>app-store-connect</string>
    <key>destination</key>
    <string>upload</string>
    <key>teamID</key>
    <string>F6ASU3CH5M</string>
    <!-- Cloud signing: Apple holds the distribution private key and signs
         server-side, so nothing but the App Store Connect API key is needed.
         No cert in the keychain, no provisioning profile on disk, nothing to
         rotate annually — which is what makes CI cheap to own.

         This file used to say the account "can't do cloud signing" and pinned
         manual signing with an explicit cert + profile. That was true of the
         key it was written against, but the cause was the key's ROLE, not the
         account. Verified 2026-08-31:

           - xcodebuild cloud signing requires an App Store Connect API key
             with the Admin role. App Manager is NOT sufficient — it fails with
             "Cloud signing permission error" / FORBIDDEN_ERROR, "You haven't
             been given access to cloud-managed distribution certificates".
           - The permission cannot be granted to a key after the fact; there is
             no UI for it. Admin keys simply have it. Re-key to fix.
           - Tested by archiving and exporting against an EMPTY temporary
             keychain (a stand-in for a clean CI runner). With the App Manager
             key the export failed; with an Admin key it produced an .ipa
             signed by "Apple Distribution: JUSTIN KEITH ROGERS (F6ASU3CH5M)"
             using an auto-generated iOS Team Store profile.

         So: if this ever regresses to "no signing certificate found", check the
         role on the key in ASC_KEY_ID before reaching for manual signing. -->
    <key>signingStyle</key>
    <string>automatic</string>
    <!-- Strip bitcode/symbols handling left at defaults; upload dSYMs. -->
    <key>uploadSymbols</key>
    <true/>
    <key>manageAppVersionAndBuildNumber</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
